// THE TWO TRANSFORM MATRICES AND THE QUANTISER'S STEPS, tabulated rather than computed.
//
// Not an optimisation - a LINKAGE constraint, and one worth stating. These are cosines, sines and
// powers of two, which would ordinarily come from `libm`; but `libm` has no shared library of its
// own in this tree, each library that wants it carries a private copy, and the dynamic graph
// refuses two libraries that export the same symbol - correctly, because two definitions of one
// name is exactly the ambiguity it exists to prevent. `vorbis` already carries that copy.
